Connecting Claude to your Gmail is a game-changer for productivity, but when it comes to giving AI access to your inbox, privacy is usually the biggest concern.

Anthropic recently rolled out native [Google Workspace connectors](https://support.claude.com/en/articles/10166901-use-google-workspace-connectors), allowing Claude to read, summarize, and draft emails directly from your chat interface.

In this guide, we'll walk through the exact, step-by-step process to set up the [Claude Gmail connector](https://claude.com/connectors/gmail) safely, and explicitly cover what Claude can (and cannot) do with your private data.

## Step-by-Step Setup Guide

Setting up the Gmail connector requires access to either the [Claude Web](https://claude.ai/) or [Claude Desktop App.](https://claude.com/download) Here is exactly how to enable it:

### 1. Open the Claude Desktop App

Launch the Claude application on your desktop.

### 2. Navigate to Connectors

Look for the **plus (+)** icon (typically next to the chat input field). Click it, then select **Connectors**. From the dropdown or menu, select **Add connectors** and then **Browse connectors**.

### 3. Initiate the Connection

Find the Google Workspace or Gmail connector in the list. Click the **+** button next to it and hit **Connect**.

### 4. Authenticate with Google

This action will automatically open a new tab in your default web browser, prompting you to choose the Gmail account you wish to connect. Select your account.

### 5. Grant Permissions

Google will ask you to review the permissions you are granting to Claude. While you can choose what you are comfortable sharing, providing the default requested permissions ensures the integration works as intended for reading and drafting.

### 6. Restart the App

Once you have granted access in the browser, return to the Claude Web App and refresh it. Or for the Desktop App, completely **close and restart** the application.

You're done! The connector is now active. You can now ask Claude to read specific emails, summarize long threads, or draft replies directly in your chat.

## Privacy & Safety: What You Need to Know

If you are concerned about safety and privacy, it is important to understand the hard limits Anthropic has placed on this integration.

Here is what Claude **cannot** do:

- **It does not read your emails proactively.** Claude only accesses your inbox when you explicitly type a prompt asking it to do so (e.g., "Summarize the latest email from John"). It is not monitoring your inbox in the background.\
- **It does not automatically send emails.** While Claude can draft a perfect reply and place it in your Gmail drafts folder, the send function is completely disabled. You must physically review and send the email yourself.\
- **It does not use your data for training.** Anthropic has confirmed that data accessed via Google Workspace connectors is not used to train their generative AI models.

### Best Practices for Sensitive Data

Even with these guardrails, it is smart to practice good digital hygiene:

#### **1. Use a Dedicated Email**

If your primary inbox contains highly sensitive legal, medical, or financial information that you absolutely do not want to expose to any third-party app, the best practice is to use a separate, dedicated email address for your AI workflows.

#### **2. The 30-Day Deletion Rule**

If you accidentally query an email containing sensitive information and want it removed from Claude's history, simply **delete the chat**.

When you delete a conversation, it is immediately removed from your UI. Anthropic's policy states that the data is then queued for complete deletion from their back-end servers, which takes up to 30 days (provided the chat wasn't flagged for safety violations).
